Z||000000||ArchMagi||08-08-2001||09:23 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.island.net/~lowell/enginethingy.jpg">  <P>What is this tube? and what is the "L" shaped plastic pipe that connects it to the rocker arm cover.  The seal on this so called pipe has broken and oil is leaking out.<P>also is it normal for oil to spill out of the filler cap when the engine is under hard load.<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>87 Base Coupe with 168,000KM<BR>4cyl, 5 speed<p>[This message has been edited by ArchMagi (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||08-08-2001||10:14 PM||||Well,I have an 84 se with 4cyl and that tube isn't on mine. I would say it is either where the crancase vent goes or maybe pcv. Mine has both. the pcv tube and valve are on the right side of the air cleaner housing but there is a hole in the valve cover with a rubber grommet and matching hole built into the snorkel. Someone who has a later mdl Duke can help out more on that. If you are losing oil out the oil filler, either the crankcase isn't vented (clogged or missing pcv), or you have a lot of blow-by. (worn or broken rings. If the pcv is hooked up and working, check the gasket on the filler cap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||08-08-2001||11:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ArchMagi:<BR><B>   <IMG SRC="http://www.island.net/~lowell/enginethingy.jpg">   <P>What is this tube? and what is the "L" shaped plastic pipe that connects it to the rocker arm cover.  The seal on this so called pipe has broken and oil is leaking out.<P>also is it normal for oil to spill out of the filler cap when the engine is under hard load.<P>Thanks<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That tube is for crankcase ventalation. <BR>It is also leaking-see below.<P>Oil out of the filler cap? Only if you have some blow-by.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Posthumane||08-09-2001||12:05 AM||||It would be possible to get oil coming out of the filler cap because of the rockers throwing some up, although more than likely you have a bit o fblowby like was mentioned.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||08-09-2001||12:35 AM||||I had some oil coming out under the filler cap on my 2.5L Fiero, especially after running through the gears at high rpms.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Turned out to be just a tired and dry seal, picked up a new cap, $2.99 fix.  Hope it's the same for you...||||reg||1
